{
  "reason": "Tier 2: separate item representations for history encoding and candidate scoring. Sampled-softmax and additional negatives failed to exceed 0.5737, while recurrent attention recovered only to 0.5713; this motivates testing representation capacity rather than further tuning candidate competition. The shared embedding receives both history-encoding and target-ranking gradients, which may conflict for directional purchase relationships, although the trajectory does not establish this as the cause.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Make one architectural change: add self.output_embedding = nn.Embedding(itemnum + 1, dim, padding_idx=0), separating candidate representations from the existing self.embedding used by encode. Initialize its weights independently with normal standard deviation 0.05 and zero its padding row; change score to normalize self.output_embedding(candidates), retaining the existing normalized features, learned scale, and jointly trained item bias. This tests whether distinct source and destination representations reduce conflicting gradients while preserving recurrent attention and the 64-negative sampled-softmax objective. Preserve GRURec.__init__, encode, score, predict, all existing attribute names, dimensions, dropout, and causal masking; both embedding tables belong to one jointly trained network per category.",
    "training_evaluation": "Update write_predict_script so working/predict.py reconstructs the modified GRURec and strictly loads its complete state dictionary, including output_embedding, from exactly one newly trained checkpoint per category. Extend check_model's existing finite-gradient and checkpoint-reload checks to cover the new parameter, without introducing additional training runs. Keep sampling, optimizer, hyperparameters, seeds, supplied splits, fixed validation candidates, checkpoint selection, deadlines, and identical validation/inference preprocessing unchanged to isolate embedding separation. Preserve train_category(name, device, deadline), write_predict_script(), predictor signatures, all four dataset routes, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, and single-GPU execution; compare actual pinned-host macro validation HR@10 against 0.5713 and 0.5737 without accessing hidden test data or combining predictors."
  }
}
